    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="1214" n="1182" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v13p1/pg1182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">S/P–NSC files, lot 62 D 1, “Indochina”</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Executive Secretary of the National
                        Security Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the NSC Planning Board</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-03-29">March 29, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>U.S. Policies with Respect to Certain Contingencies in Indochina</item>
                </list>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>References:</head>
                    <item>A. NSC 5405<anchor n="1" xml:id="d657-f1"
                        /></item>
                    <item>B. NSC Actions 1019-b, 1074<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d657-f2"/></item>
                    <item>C. Memo for Planning Board, March 26, 1954<anchor n="3" xml:id="d657-f3"
                        /></item>
                </list>
                <p>The enclosed Special Annex on Indochina, originally distributed December 31,
                    1953, and subsequently recalled, is re-circulated in a <pb facs="1215" n="1183"
                        xml:id="pg1183"/> limited number of copies for the use of the Planning Board
                    in its current consideration of the subject.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">It is requested that special security precautions be
                        observed in the handling of the enclosure and that access to it be very
                        strictly limited on an absolute need-to-know basis</hi>. All copies of the
                    enclosure will be recalled when the Planning Board completes its work on the
                    subject.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James S.
                                Lay, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d657-a1.xml" xpointer="d657-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d657-f1" n="1" xml:id="d657-f1-content">
                <p>Dated Jan. 16; for extracts, see <ref target="#pg971">p. 971</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d657-f2" n="2" xml:id="d657-f2-content">
                <p>NSC Action No. 1019 is included in extracts from
                    the memorandum of discussion at the 181st Meeting of the National Security
                    Council, Jan. 21, <ref target="#pg986">p. 986</ref>. For Action No. 1074, see
                    extracts from the memorandum of discussion at the 190th Meeting of the Council,
                    Mar. 25, <ref target="#pg1163">p. 1163</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d657-f3" n="3" xml:id="d657-f3-content">
                <p>Reference is to a memorandum by NSC Executive
                    Secretary Lay to the NSC Planning Board, Mar. 26, transmitting a list of
                    points made in Council discussion and an analysis of the problem by General
                        Cutler, Special Assistant to the
                    President for National Security Affairs. The memorandum and its enclosure are
                    not printed. (S/P–NSC files, lot 62 D 1, “Indochina”)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
